title: 'subscribe-daemon/WS client: cancel mid-connect must close sockets (FD leak under 502)'
updated_at: "2026-07-23T08:51:31Z"
---
## Problem
Registration uses `Lwt.pick [ run_alias_connection; conn_cancel ]`. If cancel wins while `create_ws_session_lwt` is mid-TLS or mid-`read_line`, the fiber is cancelled. It is not proven that `Tls_lwt` / `Lwt_io` always free the underlying FD; live measurement (FD 596→693 and ESTAB 105→193 in 10s under 502) is consistent with leaked or overlapping in-flight connects.

Also: `connect_subscribe` only closes on the exception path after `open_channels` returns — cancel mid-handshake can skip cleanup.

## Solution
1. Structure connect with `Lwt.finalize` around open channels so cancel/timeout always closes the socket.
2. Ensure deregister/cleanup_client cancel path cannot leave orphan ESTAB sockets.
3. Regression: cancel mid-connect does not grow `/proc/self/fd` across many iterations.

## Files
- `ocaml/relay_ws_client.ml`
- `ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml`

